# Q58 (the author, 2026-10-01): `Batch: (put: 7)` with put a method of the unit -- Batch, absent, holds the one
# Structure (put: 7): the known call is RETAINED as a statement of Batch's body, not executed at the definition, and
# runs when Batch is executed (the bare atom).  put counts its calls in the unit's field through the explicit path
# node\hits (Q52: a bare write would change only its hidden input), and count reads that cell the same way --
# the root's own bare `hits` is its working value, not reloaded after a call (§7b).  0 after the definition, 1 after
# `Batch`.  Was "unresolved name": a tail of one known call was read as the head's value.  Success is 7.
int: hits 0
fn: put (int: n) int
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
    return: n
end: put
Batch: (put: 7)
fn: count () int
return: node\hits
int: before count()
Batch
int: after count()
int: ok 0
if: before = 0 && after = 1
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
